    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Model deployments\r\n\r\n**Azure Resource Graph cannot see model deployments.** The type\r\n`microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/deployments` returns zero rows - this was\r\nmeasured against live deployments, not assumed.\r\n\r\nThis tab uses the **Azure Resource Manager** control plane, which returns deployments\r\nfor **one account at a time**. Click a row in the account list below to switch\r\naccounts, or use the **Model account** parameter at the top.\r\n\r\n> **Seeing an empty grid?** That usually means the selected account genuinely hosts\r\n> no models. **Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)** accounts are frequently used for\r\n> Document Intelligence, Speech or Vision rather than model hosting, so they\r\n> legitimately have zero deployments. Azure OpenAI accounts are therefore listed and\r\n> selected first. Try another account, or run `Get-AIModelRetirement.ps1` for a\r\n> fleet-wide sweep.\r\n\r\n> **Why not all accounts at once?** Workbook ARM queries only accept a single Azure\r\n> *resource* path - a tenant-level `POST /batch` is rejected with\r\n> *\"Path must be for an Azure Resource\"*, and a multi-value parameter is joined\r\n> into one malformed path rather than fanned out. Both were tested against the\r\n> live portal. `Get-AIModelRetirement.ps1` batches the same calls across every\r\n> subscription and computes days-to-retirement per deployment.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "mdHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| where kind in~ ('OpenAI','AIServices')\n| extend kindRank = iff(kind =~ 'OpenAI', 0, 1)\n| project\n    Account = name,\n    Kind = iff(kind =~ 'OpenAI', 'Azure OpenAI', 'Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)'),\n    ['Resource group'] = resourceGroup,\n    Region = location,\n    SKU = tostring(sku.name),\n    State = tostring(properties.provisioningState),\n    Endpoint = tostring(properties.endpoint),\n    kindRank,\n    ResourceId = id\n| order by kindRank asc, Account asc\n| project-away kindRank",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model-hosting accounts (click a row to load its deployments)",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscriptions}"
              ],
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "exportParameterName": "ModelAccounts",
              "exportDefaultValue": "",
              "exportFieldName": "ResourceId",
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "Modelhostingaccountsclickarowtoloaditsdeployments"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Deployments for the selected account\r\n\r\n* **Version upgrade policy** - `NoAutoUpgrade` means the deployment will **not**\r\n  move off a retiring model version on its own. Those are your migration risks.\r\n  `OnceCurrentVersionExpired` auto-upgrades only at expiry;\r\n  `OnceNewDefaultVersionAvailable` tracks the current default.\r\n* **Content filter** - a deployment with no RAI policy is unfiltered.\r\n* **SKU** - `Standard` / `GlobalStandard` are pay-as-you-go; `ProvisionedManaged` is reserved capacity.\r\n\r\nThis grid is the authoritative response from the selected account's\r\n`/deployments` endpoint: **one row per actual deployment**. It deliberately does not\r\nmerge the model catalog into this table. Azure Workbooks supports only one join key,\r\nand composite JSONPath keys can evaluate empty in some portal runtimes, producing a\r\ncross join where every deployment is repeated for every catalog model.\r\n\r\nUse **Model retirement** for the live regional lifecycle calendar. For a fleet-wide\r\ndeployment-to-retirement join with days remaining, run\r\n**`Get-AIModelRetirement.ps1`**.\r\n\r\n**Two things to expect:**\r\n\r\n* An empty grid means the selected account has no model deployments. This is normal\r\n  for AI Services accounts used for Document Intelligence, Speech, or Vision.\r\n* **Tick exactly one account.** Azure Workbooks send an ARM query to **one Azure\r\n  resource path at a time** - `GET` and `GETARRAY` were both tested and each joins\r\n  multiple selected values into a single malformed path, and there is no\r\n  subscription-wide deployments API. Selecting several accounts will error."
            },
            "name": "mdWhat"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "{\"version\":\"ARMEndpoint/1.0\",\"method\":\"GET\",\"path\":\"{ModelAccounts}/deployments\",\"headers\":[],\"urlParams\":[{\"key\":\"api-version\",\"value\":\"2024-10-01\"}],\"batchDisabled\":false,\"transformers\":[{\"type\":\"jsonpath\",\"settings\":{\"tablePath\":\"$.value[*]\",\"columns\":[{\"path\":\"name\",\"columnid\":\"Deployment\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.name\",\"columnid\":\"Model\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.version\",\"columnid\":\"Version\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.model.format\",\"columnid\":\"Format\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"sku.name\",\"columnid\":\"SKU\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"sku.capacity\",\"columnid\":\"Capacity\",\"columnType\":\"number\"},{\"path\":\"properties.versionUpgradeOption\",\"columnid\":\"Version upgrade policy\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.raiPolicyName\",\"columnid\":\"Content filter\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"properties.provisioningState\",\"columnid\":\"State\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"id\",\"columnid\":\"Resource ID\",\"columnType\":\"string\"}]}}]}",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model deployments",
              "queryType": 12,
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "ModelDeployments"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "models"
      },
      "name": "group-models"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Model retirement calendar\r\n\r\nLive retirement dates straight from the Azure model catalog, via the Resource\r\nManager control plane. Nothing here is hard-coded, so the dates stay correct as\r\nMicrosoft updates them.\r\n\r\nThe catalog shown is for the **region, subscription and account kind of the account\r\ncurrently selected on the Model deployments tab** - pick a different account there to\r\nsee a different catalog.\r\n\r\n> **Why the kind filter matters.** Azure returns the catalog once **per account kind**,\r\n> so the same model is listed several times - `gpt-4.1` appears once as `OpenAI` and\r\n> again as `AIServices` with identical dates. Unfiltered, a single region returned\r\n> **167 duplicated rows**. This grid is filtered to the selected account's kind, which\r\n> removes the duplicates and shows exactly the models **that account** can run.\r\n\r\n**How to use this tab**\r\n\r\n1. Note each model + version you actually run on the **Model deployments** tab.\r\n2. Find that model + version below to get its **Inference retirement** date.\r\n3. Prioritise any deployment whose **Version upgrade policy** is `NoAutoUpgrade` -\r\n   those will not migrate themselves.\r\n\r\n**Lifecycle meanings**\r\n\r\n| Status | Meaning |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| `GenerallyAvailable` | Supported for production |\r\n| `Preview` | Not for production; can be retired at short notice |\r\n| `Deprecating` | Retirement scheduled - **new deployments are already blocked** |\r\n| `Deprecated` | Retired - existing deployments stop serving traffic |\r\n\r\nAzure blocks new deployments of deprecating/deprecated versions, but **existing\r\ndeployments keep running until the retirement date and then fail**. That gap is\r\nexactly what this tab is for.\r\n\r\nFor a computed, fleet-wide report with days-remaining and severity across every\r\nsubscription, run `Get-AIModelRetirement.ps1`.",
              "style": "warning"
            },
            "name": "rtHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "{\"version\":\"ARMEndpoint/1.0\",\"method\":\"GET\",\"path\":\"subscriptions/{AccountSubscription}/providers/Microsoft.CognitiveServices/locations/{AccountRegion}/models\",\"headers\":[],\"urlParams\":[{\"key\":\"api-version\",\"value\":\"2024-10-01\"}],\"batchDisabled\":false,\"transformers\":[{\"type\":\"jsonpath\",\"settings\":{\"tablePath\":\"$.value[?(@.kind == '{AccountKind}')]\",\"columns\":[{\"path\":\"model.name\",\"columnid\":\"Model\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.version\",\"columnid\":\"Version\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.format\",\"columnid\":\"Format\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.lifecycleStatus\",\"columnid\":\"Lifecycle\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.deprecation.inference\",\"columnid\":\"Inference retirement\",\"columnType\":\"datetime\"},{\"path\":\"model.deprecation.fineTune\",\"columnid\":\"Fine-tune retirement\",\"columnType\":\"datetime\"},{\"path\":\"kind\",\"columnid\":\"Account kind\",\"columnType\":\"string\"},{\"path\":\"model.maxCapacity\",\"columnid\":\"Max capacity\",\"columnType\":\"number\"}]}}]}",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Model catalog and retirement dates",
              "queryType": 12,
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true,
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Lifecycle",
                    "formatter": 18,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "thresholdsOptions": "colors",
                      "thresholdsGrid": [
                        {
                          "operator": "is Empty",
                          "representation": "red",
                          "text": "Not in catalog (retired/legacy)"
                        },
                        {
                          "operator": "==",
                          "thresholdValue": "Deprecating",
                          "representation": "redBright",
                          "text": "{0}{1}"
                        },
                        {
                          "operator": "==",
                          "thresholdValue": "Deprecated",
                          "representation": "red",
                          "text": "{0}{1}"
                        },
                        {
                          "operator": "==",
                          "thresholdValue": "Preview",
                          "representation": "orange",
                          "text": "{0}{1}"
                        },
                        {
                          "operator": "==",
                          "thresholdValue": "GenerallyAvailable",
                          "representation": "green",
                          "text": "{0}{1}"
                        },
                        {
                          "operator": "Default",
                          "representation": "gray",
                          "text": "{0}{1}"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "name": "Modelcatalogandretirementdates"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "retire"
      },
      "name": "group-retire"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Account security and network posture\r\n\r\nEvery column is backed by a property that Resource Graph genuinely populates for\r\n`microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts`. This was confirmed by setting each field\r\nthrough ARM and re-reading it in Resource Graph - so a blank value means\r\n*not configured*, never *not indexed*."
            },
            "name": "poHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| extend acctKind   = tostring(kind)\n| extend isModelHost = (acctKind in~ ('OpenAI','AIServices'))\n| extend skuName    = tostring(sku.name)\n| extend identityType = tostring(identity.type)\n| extend pna        = tostring(properties.publicNetworkAccess)\n| extend localAuthDisabled = tobool(properties.disableLocalAuth)\n| extend subdomain  = tostring(properties.customSubDomainName)\n| extend restrictOutbound = tobool(properties.restrictOutboundNetworkAccess)\n| extend netDefault = tostring(properties.networkAcls.defaultAction)\n| extend ipRuleCount = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.networkAcls.ipRules)))\n| extend vnetRuleCount = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.networkAcls.virtualNetworkRules)))\n| extend cmkSource  = tostring(properties.encryption.keySource)\n| extend allowProjectMgmt = tobool(properties.allowProjectManagement)\n| extend state      = tostring(properties.provisioningState)\n| extend created    = todatetime(properties.dateCreated)\n| extend endpoint   = tostring(properties.endpoint)\n| extend isMigrated = tobool(properties.isMigrated)\n| extend peCount    = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.privateEndpointConnections)))\n| extend KindLabel  = case(\n      acctKind =~ 'OpenAI',     'Azure OpenAI',\n      acctKind =~ 'AIServices', 'Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)',\n      acctKind =~ 'CognitiveServices', 'Cognitive Services (multi-service)',\n      acctKind)\n| project\n    Account = name,\n    Kind = KindLabel,\n    ['Resource group'] = resourceGroup,\n    ['Entra ID only'] = case(isnull(localAuthDisabled), 'Unknown', localAuthDisabled == true, 'Yes', 'No - API keys allowed'),\n    ['Managed identity'] = iff(isempty(identityType) or identityType =~ 'None', 'None', identityType),\n    ['Custom subdomain'] = iff(isempty(subdomain), 'Not set', subdomain),\n    ['Encryption'] = iff(isempty(cmkSource) or cmkSource =~ 'Microsoft.CognitiveServices', 'Microsoft-managed', cmkSource),\n    ResourceId = id\n| order by ['Entra ID only'] desc, Account asc",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Authentication and encryption",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscriptions}"
              ],
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "Authenticationandencryption"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| extend acctKind   = tostring(kind)\n| extend isModelHost = (acctKind in~ ('OpenAI','AIServices'))\n| extend skuName    = tostring(sku.name)\n| extend identityType = tostring(identity.type)\n| extend pna        = tostring(properties.publicNetworkAccess)\n| extend localAuthDisabled = tobool(properties.disableLocalAuth)\n| extend subdomain  = tostring(properties.customSubDomainName)\n| extend restrictOutbound = tobool(properties.restrictOutboundNetworkAccess)\n| extend netDefault = tostring(properties.networkAcls.defaultAction)\n| extend ipRuleCount = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.networkAcls.ipRules)))\n| extend vnetRuleCount = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.networkAcls.virtualNetworkRules)))\n| extend cmkSource  = tostring(properties.encryption.keySource)\n| extend allowProjectMgmt = tobool(properties.allowProjectManagement)\n| extend state      = tostring(properties.provisioningState)\n| extend created    = todatetime(properties.dateCreated)\n| extend endpoint   = tostring(properties.endpoint)\n| extend isMigrated = tobool(properties.isMigrated)\n| extend peCount    = toint(array_length(todynamic(properties.privateEndpointConnections)))\n| extend KindLabel  = case(\n      acctKind =~ 'OpenAI',     'Azure OpenAI',\n      acctKind =~ 'AIServices', 'Microsoft Foundry (AI Services)',\n      acctKind =~ 'CognitiveServices', 'Cognitive Services (multi-service)',\n      acctKind)\n| project\n    Account = name,\n    Kind = KindLabel,\n    ['Public access'] = iff(isempty(pna), 'Unknown', pna),\n    ['Network default action'] = iff(isempty(netDefault), 'Allow (not configured)', netDefault),\n    ['IP rules'] = coalesce(ipRuleCount, 0),\n    ['VNet rules'] = coalesce(vnetRuleCount, 0),\n    ['Private endpoints'] = coalesce(peCount, 0),\n    ['Outbound restricted'] = case(isnull(restrictOutbound), 'No', restrictOutbound == true, 'Yes', 'No'),\n    Endpoint = endpoint,\n    ResourceId = id\n| order by ['Private endpoints'] asc, Account asc",
              "size": 2,
              "title": "Network exposure",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscriptions}"
              ],
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "gridSettings": {
                "rowLimit": 1000,
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "Networkexposure"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "posture"
      },
      "name": "group-posture"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## Microsoft Foundry projects\r\n\r\nFoundry projects (`microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/projects`) **are** indexed\r\nby Resource Graph. Each project inherits its parent Foundry account's\r\nauthentication and network configuration, so the parent's posture is joined in below."
            },
            "name": "fdHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/projects'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| summarize Projects = count(), Accounts = dcount(tostring(split(name, '/')[0]))\n| extend Tiles = pack_array(\n    pack('Metric', 'Foundry projects', 'Value', Projects, 'Rank', 1),\n    pack('Metric', 'Foundry accounts hosting projects', 'Value', Accounts, 'Rank', 2))\n| mv-expand Tiles\n| project Metric = tostring(Tiles.Metric), Value = toint(Tiles.Value), Rank = toint(Tiles.Rank)\n| order by Rank asc",
              "size": 3,
              "title": "Foundry project summary",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscriptions}"
              ],
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "tileSettings": {
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                },
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "auto"
                  },
                  "numberFormat": {
                    "unit": 17,
                    "options": {
                      "style": "decimal",
                      "maximumFractionDigits": 0
                    }
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "sortCriteriaField": "Rank",
                "sortOrderField": 1
              }
            },
            "name": "Foundryprojectsummary"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/projects'\n| extend _rgs = dynamic([{ResourceGroups}])\n| where array_length(_rgs) == 0 or set_has_element(_rgs, '*') or set_has_element(_rgs, resourceGroup)\n| extend accountName = tostring(split(name, '/')[0])\n| extend projectName = tostring(split(name, '/')[-1])\n| extend parentId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(id, '/projects/')))\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts'\n    | project parentId = tolower(id), parentPna = tostring(properties.publicNetworkAccess),\n              parentLocalAuth = tobool(properties.disableLocalAuth)\n  ) on parentId\n| project\n    Project = projectName,\n    ['Foundry account'] = accountName,\n    ['Resource group'] = resourceGroup,\n    Region = location,\n    ['Display name'] = tostring(properties.displayName),\n    ['Is default'] = iff(tobool(properties.isDefault) == true, 'Yes', 'No'),\n    ['Managed identity'] = iff(isempty(tostring(identity.type)) or tostring(identity.type) =~ 'None', 'None', tostring(identity.type)),\n    State = tostring(properties.provisioningState),\n    ['Parent public access'] = iff(isempty(parentPna), 'Unknown', parentPna),\n    ['Parent Entra ID only'] = case(isnull(parentLocalAuth), 'Unknown', parentLocalAuth == true, 'Yes', 'No'),\n    ResourceId = id\n| order by ['Foundry account'] asc, Project asc",
              "size": 2,
